Vendored material under `references/` retains its own original license and
attribution — see each subfolder's `VENDORED.txt` for terms; do not assume
MIT applies there. This MIT license covers this repository's own content only
(research notes, guides, workflows, catalog, and the `tooling/` templates).

**Note on two vendored subfolders:** `references/anthropic-skills/` and
`references/claude-code-plugins/` are vendored from Anthropic repositories
that carry no repo-root open-source license as of the vendor date (checked
via GitHub's license API) — their terms are not confirmed open. If
redistributing this repo publicly, verify Anthropic's actual terms for that
content first, or exclude those two subfolders from the public copy.
